<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tafari Benti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Teferi Bante</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tafari Benti (1921–1977) was an Ethiopian army general who became chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derg">Derg</a>, the military council that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a>, and thus head of state in November 1974. Largely a figurehead, he was killed in a shoot-out at a Derg meeting in February 1977, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mengistu-haile-mariam">Mengistu Haile Mariam</a> took full power.</p></div>
